er good books and there's so much  research to be done that we don't know  yet that we even need to do  so i think the problem is i would like  to branch out i was wanted to have  copies i want to be uploaded and be able  to have not just backup copies but  parallel copies  because the universe  is really rich it's much more complex  than a single mind can understand and  even a collective of mine is unable to  truly understand it because it's a  universe containing collectives of mind  making complicated art complicated  thoughts that is of course by nature  just as complex as what we're thinking  so we are always going to be struggling  for prioritizing of understanding and  creating more creating art creating  games creating new little virtual worlds  creating big virtual worlds simulating  the past present and future  so what i want to do if i get an  arbitrary amount of time is of course  adding to the universe  it's such an interesting universe but i  think we can make it even better  a lot of philosophers have argued that  our sort of mortality our finitude is  part of what gives life meaning people  like heidegger and thinking even bernard  williams in the paper called the  markopoulos case  do you think they're wrong about that do  you think it isn't mortality that sort  of gives human life its meaning i i  think it's a mistake i think it's a bit  like arguing that it's divorce that give  makes love have meaning  in some sense yes the fine attitude and  the risk adds a particular spice and  structure to it  but i think the most important aspect is  that everything is in some sense mortal  because eventually the proton decay or  the heat depth of the universe will get  every form of structure there is  very very very very far in the future  but if i were to live for a billion year  or 10 years  from a heideggerian perspective does  that matter  that perspective actually doesn't  include an explicit uh measure of time  it's just the fact that my life is  finite that matters but that's going to  be fine that even if i'm opposed human  who's going to live for trillions of  years i'm still going to have to face  eventually that my black hole power  systems are going to run out in some icy  very dark age in the far future  and in that case i'm just as mortal as a  mayfly from the perspective of infinite  but normally we care about what we fill  the time with  normally we might say that a long rich  life is better than a short rich life  because there was more rich moments  there was more other things and i do  think they add up  but different people might live very  different structures over life there are  some people who format their lives in a  very different way from what i might do  and they might actually say yeah i don't  need more than this amount of time and  then i'm done well i think right now  given how i'm functioning i would just  add more and more goals and we kind of  get stressed oh no it's only a 50  trillion years on the heater for the  universe and i hardly start that  andersenberg thank you very much thank  you  for more debates talks and interviews  subscribe today to the institute of art  and ideas at iai tv  [Music]  you
 

